<title>USA: U. Michigan consumer sentiment 104.6 May prelim.</title>
<headline>U. Michigan consumer sentiment 104.6 May prelim.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The University of Michigan's preliminary index of consumer sentiment for May rose to 104.6 from 101.4 in the final April index, financial market sources said Friday.</p>
<p>The current conditions component fell to 113.9 from 115.2, while the expectations index rose to 98.6 from 92.5, the sources said.</p>
<p>The data are released only to paying subscribers.</p>
<p>((--N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
